Cycles: render without denoising when no denoiser is available

The factory startup scene has final-render denoising on with OpenImageDenoise. In a build without
OIDN (Haiku arm64: no OIDN port yet) every F12 and `blender -b -f` render of it stopped with "Error:
Build without OpenImageDenoiser" (in background mode Blender quits). The viewport already falls back
to no denoising when no denoiser is available; final renders now do the same (sync.cpp), and the
add-on does not register the "Noisy Image" pass then (engine.py): with denoising off it would be the
same noisy pass as "Combined", and the saved image came out black.

diff --git a/intern/cycles/blender/addon/engine.py b/intern/cycles/blender/addon/engine.py
index 6a28582..e705a01 100644
--- a/intern/cycles/blender/addon/engine.py
+++ b/intern/cycles/blender/addon/engine.py
@@ -171,6 +171,14 @@ def system_info():
     return _cycles.system_info()
 
 
+def denoising_available(scene):
+    # Without OpenImageDenoise (and without OptiX) a final render runs without denoising (sync.cpp,
+    # get_denoise_params()): no denoised result, so no separate "Noisy Image" pass either — with one, it
+    # and "Combined" would be the same noisy pass and the saved image came out black.
+    import _cycles
+    return _cycles.with_openimagedenoise or scene.cycles.denoiser == 'OPTIX'
+
+
 def list_render_passes(scene, srl):
     import _cycles
 
@@ -230,7 +238,7 @@ def list_render_passes(scene, srl):
             yield ("CryptoAsset" + '{:02d}'.format(i), "rgba", 'COLOR')
 
     # Denoising passes.
-    if scene.cycles.use_denoising and crl.use_denoising:
+    if scene.cycles.use_denoising and crl.use_denoising and denoising_available(scene):
         yield ("Noisy Image", "RGBA", 'COLOR')
         if crl.use_pass_shadow_catcher:
             yield ("Noisy Shadow Catcher", "RGB", 'COLOR')
diff --git a/intern/cycles/blender/sync.cpp b/intern/cycles/blender/sync.cpp
index 14d79c5..d4ef296 100644
--- a/intern/cycles/blender/sync.cpp
+++ b/intern/cycles/blender/sync.cpp
@@ -994,6 +994,14 @@ DenoiseParams BlenderSync::get_denoise_params(BL::Scene &b_scene,
     }
   }
 
+  /* A build without OpenImageDenoise (or a CPU it does not support) renders without denoising, as the
+   * viewport's automatic choice does, instead of stopping the render with "Build without
+   * OpenImageDenoiser": the factory startup scene has final-render denoising on. The add-on then
+   * registers no "Noisy Image" pass either (engine.py, denoising_available()). */
+  if (denoising.use && denoising.type != DENOISER_OPTIX && !openimagedenoise_supported()) {
+    denoising.use = false;
+  }
+
   switch (input_passes) {
     case DENOISER_INPUT_RGB:
       denoising.use_pass_albedo = false;
